 Nifty Trading Plan for October 19, 2026 
 Nifty may advance towards its immediate target zone of 23,300–23,350
 Sustainability of the uptrend remains a key factor to watch
 On the downside, immediate support is placed in the 22,900–23,000 range
 Did our AI summary help? 
 Market Mastery
With momentum indicators showing further improvement and the Nifty 50 trading decisively above its short-term moving averages, the index may advance towards its immediate target zone of 23,300–23,350. However, the sustainability of the uptrend remains a key factor to watch, as the broader technical structure is still weak and crude oil prices remain elevated. On the downside, immediate support is placed in the 22,900–23,000 range. Meanwhile, the Bank Nifty needs to decisively clear the 56,100 hurdle to extend its upmove towards 56,500. Until then, the index may continue to consolidate, with immediate support at 55,500, followed by 55,300. A breach of the 55,300 level could prompt market participants to turn cautious, experts said.
On October 16, the Nifty 50 rallied 149 points, or 0.65 percent, to close at 23,146, while the Bank Nifty gained 34 points, or 0.06 percent, to end at 55,844. Market breadth on the NSE remained positive, with 1,894 shares advancing against 1,345 declining.
 Jatin Gedia, Technical Research Analyst, VP, Derivatives & Technical Research at Teji Mandi 
Nifty formed a strong bullish candle on the weekly charts surpassing and closing above the previous two-week high (23,080). It has formed a Morning Star kind of candlestick pattern, which is a three-candlestick reversal pattern. It respected the 50-month exponential moving average (22,096) which was violated only on two previous occasions: once in 2008 and again in 2020. This is significant because subsequent dips towards this average have been bought, and the current dip towards that average has also been bought, suggesting a resumption of the primary uptrend.
The rise from 22,179 has been impulsive, suggesting the bottom is in place according to Elliott Wave principles. In terms of price pattern it has broken out from an inverted head and shoulders pattern which is a trend reversal pattern. On the upside, the immediate hurdle is at 23,477 - 23,500 which coincides with the 50 percent retracement level of the entire decline from 24,774 to 22,179. Immediate support is at 22,800 - 22,850, based on the role reversal principle.
 Strategy : Buy Nifty October Futures at around 23,119, with a stop-loss of 23,030, and target of 23,400.
 Hitesh Rathi, Technical Analyst (Equity & Derivatives) at Angel One 
On the weekly chart, a well-defined range has emerged, with the upside capped near the 24,000 mark, which aligns closely with the 20-WEMA and continues to act as a formidable resistance zone. On the downside, the index remains well supported in the 23,200–23,100 band. The shorter-term setup suggests that a move above the 23,550 mark could trigger fresh upside momentum.
On the other hand, a breakdown below the 23,200–23,100 support zone is likely to shift the balance in favour of the bears, paving the way for further selling pressure and opening the door for a potential decline towards the 22,700 level.
That said, the repeated defence of the lower support band clearly indicates the presence of strong demand at lower levels and tilts the scales marginally in favour of the bulls.
 Strategy : Buy Nifty Futures near 23,000 with a stop-loss of 22,900 and book profits near 23,200-23,250.
 Hitesh Rathi, Technical Analyst (Equity & Derivatives) at Angel One 
The second consecutive week of gains marks a healthy development for the high-beta Bank Nifty index, reflecting an improvement in the underlying market structure. Private sector banks led the constructive momentum throughout the week, contributing positively to overall sentiment.
From a technical perspective, the index has reclaimed its 20-DEMA and is now positioned marginally below the bearish gap on the daily chart. On the upside, the gap around 56,200 is likely to act as an intermediate hurdle. A decisive breakout above this zone could pave the way towards the 56,600 subzone, where notable rejections have been observed in recent history.
On the downside, the improving trend structure is expected to provide support during any declines towards the 55,200-55,000 subzone. However, the crucial support remains firmly placed around the 54,500-54,450 zone, which is essential to sustain the positive outlook.
 Strategy : Buy Bank Nifty Futures near 55,600 with a stop-loss of 55,250, and book profits near the 56,000 mark.
 Jatin Gedia, Technical Research Analyst, VP, Derivatives & Technical Research at Teji Mandi 
